and give you a very meaningful behind-the-scenes experience.

12
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Our activity today will officially start.

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
First of all, I would like to invite our Chinese team teacher, Sherry,

14
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
to bring you the new features of Marvelous Design 12.

15
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Let's give a round of applause to Sherry.

16
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Good afternoon, everyone.

17
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
I believe that some of you may have seen me for the first time.

18
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
I am Sherry, who is always hiding behind the screen.

19
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Today, I will share with you the new features of Marvelous Design 12.

20
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
How many of you have used Marvelous Design 12 before?

21
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:37,000
It seems that our new features introduction is very necessary.

22
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:45,000
In Marvelous Design 12, the first new feature that we have introduced is the auto-design of the clothes.

23
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:53,000
In the previous version of Marvelous Design, we have introduced the auto-design of the clothes and the auto-adjustment of the pieces.

24
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:01,000
These features need to be built on our clothes or on the virtual models to have the information of the clothes.

25
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:09,000
So in the previous version, we need to manually create the clothes for our new virtual models.

26
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:16,000
In the new version, first of all, in the past, we could not directly see the information of the clothes.

27
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Now, in the 3D window, we can directly display the clothes of the clothes.

28
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:27,000
When we start displaying the clothes of the clothes, there will be a red grid next to it.

29
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
These grids are the information of the clothes that the clothes have.

30
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Usually, the transformation or wearing of the clothes is based on the information of the clothes.

31
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Now, when we import the virtual model of the OBJ model, we can select the auto-design of the clothes.

32
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:51,000
After our short calculation and simulation, the virtual model will bring the information of the clothes itself.

33
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,000
We can click on the display of the virtual model of the clothes.

34
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
We can see that there is a black grid around it, which is the information of the clothes it has.

35
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Now, after we directly click on the auto-adjustment of the pieces, the clothes will automatically change according to the information of the clothes.

36
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
We do not need to manually create the clothes anymore.

37
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:20,000
In addition to the fact that the OBJ model can automatically create the clothes,

38
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:25,000
the FBX model can also automatically create the clothes.

39
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:32,000
However, one thing we need to pay attention to is that the information of the clothes

40
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:38,000
needs to ensure that the virtual model has a head when it is automatically created.

41
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,000
If the virtual model you import does not have a head,

42
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,000
then there is no way for it to automatically create the clothes.

43
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:49,000
The second new feature is the model line tool group.

44
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:56,000
When we choose to create and edit the model line tool,

45
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:02,000
our clothes will change from the original material or color to a white draft model.

46
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:06,000
At this time, we can directly edit clothes in 3D space,

47
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:10,000
instead of editing clothes in 2D window like before.

48
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:14,000
When we use the edit model line tool to drag the point,

49
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,000
you can see that the 2D and 3D window are modified simultaneously.

50
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
And when we modify a point,

51
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:24,000
other points and lines that are linked to it will be modified at the same time.

52
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,000
If we drag the line in 3D space,

53
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,000
you can see that the line will change infinitely.

54
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:43,000
So now we can not only edit clothes in 2D window,

55
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,000
but we can also edit clothes in 3D window.

56
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Next, there is another feature called the model line tool group.

57
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,000
When we create a dress,

58
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:57,000
it is very convenient to use the model line tool to change the width of the dress.

59
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,000
For example, now I can change the width of the dress,

60
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,000
or if I want to shrink the dress,

61
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
I can shrink the dress.

62
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,000
This is the model line tool group.

63
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:12,000
In addition to using the model line tool group to change the dress,

64
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:17,000
we can also use the model line tool to modify the sleeves.

65
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:23,000
For example, now I can shrink the sleeves.

66
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:32,000
So now it is very convenient for us to modify these model lines in 3D window.

67
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:35,000
The next one is the mobile model line.

68
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:38,000
The mobile model line is a very common function

69
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
when we modify the side seam line of the dress,

70
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
or to adjust the length of the dress.

71
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,000
For example, sometimes we will feel that the side seam line,

72
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
if we move it forward or backward,

73
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:52,000
we can drag the side seam line directly into the 3D window,

74
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
which is the mobile model line.

75
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,000
It will also be modified in conjunction.

76
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:00,000
For example, if we move it backwards,

77
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,000
the front will become wider and the back will become narrower.

78
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,000
If we want to modify the length of the dress,

79
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
we will also use the mobile model line function.

80
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,000
If we drag the model line downwards,

81
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:19,000
the whole bottom line will be modified along the original side seam line.

82
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
It is not moved directly.

83
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
There is also the custom model line.

84
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
In fact, the custom model line,

85
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:29,000
because our model line is actually the outline of the panel,

86
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:33,000
so when we use the custom model line to cut,

87
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:37,000
we will see that the panel will automatically be cut.

88
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
If we click on the panel,

89
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,000
OK,

90
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:46,000
there will be a curve on the panel.

91
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
And after we finish drawing,

92
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
the panel will automatically be cut down,

93
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
and there will be a line.

94
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,000
So this function,

95
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:59,000
we will usually use it to make the cut and shape of the dress.

96
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:06,000
All of the operations of our creative styling line are symmetrical.

97
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
So as long as we draw one side,

98
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
the other side will automatically be symmetrical.

99
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:17,000
This function is actually for everyone to use in 3D window editing.

100
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:21,000
The next new function is to create a spiral version.

101
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Now we can see the left and right sides of the dress created.

102
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,000
Its harmony effect is different.

103
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,000
When we make a lot of dresses,

104
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:31,000
we will need to use the ones on the right,

105
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:35,000
which are more viscous and have a richer fold.

106
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,000
And on the left side,

107
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:39,000
because we originally used a rectangular version,

108
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,000
its length difference is not enough.

109
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
So its fold is not large enough.

110
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,000
For a rectangular version,

111
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,000
it has a feature,

112
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,000
that is,

113
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,000
its length difference is relatively large.

114
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
For example,

115
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
its inner circle may be 120 cm,

116
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,000
and the outer circle is 180 cm.

117
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,000
In the middle,

118
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
there will be a 60 cm difference.

119
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
This difference will be reflected on the edge.

120
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Because of this difference,

121
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,000
the fold of the edge here will become more.

122
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
So sometimes,

123
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,000
when we sew the edge of the contract,

124
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,000
we use a rectangular version.

125
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Sometimes,

126
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,000
it looks like it has a lot of fold,

127
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,000
but it is not.

128
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
If the fold is not very obvious,

129
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
we can use this

130
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
rectangular version

131
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
to complete the effect we want.

132
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,000
Now,

133
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,000
when choosing to create a rectangular version,

134
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
we will have to fill in some numbers.

135
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
The first number is the radius.

136
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
If you don't know what this radius is,

137
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,000
actually,

138
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,000
when we modify this number,

139
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
there will be a light blue reference line.

140
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
This reference line tells us,

141
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,000
for example,

142
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
the first radius,

143
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
it is the radius from the center of our rectangle

144
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
to the starting position of our rectangle.

145
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
The smaller this number is,

146
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
the more the starting position of our rectangle is.

147
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
The next one is the length.

148
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:56,000
The length is the length of the side of our rectangle.

149
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:01,000
The inner side and the outer side are relative,

150
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
so if we change one of the numbers,

151
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:06,000
the other number will be modified in conjunction.

152
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Usually,

153
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
our inner value

154
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,000
will match the length of

155
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
the horizontal row of our rectangle

156
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,000
or the horizontal row of our rectangle.

157
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,000
Now,

158
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
let's check the width of the side.

159
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
This side is the width of the rectangle.

160
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
The inner side is the length of the yellow line

161
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,000
on the inner side.

162
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
The outer side is the length of the yellow line

163
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
on the outer side.

164
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,000
This is the kind of shape

165
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:39,440
All you have to do is to understand the width of the edge of the river.

166
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:44,360
Our width can be set to a different value.

167
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,799
Next is the diameter.

168
00:09:45,799 --> 00:09:55,360
Dismantle is the diameter of each circle of our spiral board.

169
00:09:55,360 --> 00:10:00,240
It should be noted that the diameter of the diameter cannot be smaller than the width of the side edge.

170
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:03,240
Otherwise, our board will cross.

171
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:08,759
If the board is crossed, the board will not be able to be created.

172
00:10:12,279 --> 00:10:15,120
Finally, the direction.

173
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:17,799
The direction can be set to a clockwise or a counterclockwise direction.

174
00:10:17,799 --> 00:10:20,919
This is based on the position of our seal.

175
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:27,600
That's all about creating a spiral board.

176
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:32,680
The next function is the resetting of the cycle.

177
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:37,799
In the previous version, for example, in Marvelous Designer 11,

178
00:10:37,799 --> 00:10:41,799
we added a smart loop tool.

179
00:10:41,799 --> 00:10:44,279
In Marvelous Designer 12,

180
00:10:44,279 --> 00:10:50,960
our smart loop can finally be created along the inner line.

181
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:54,279
The problem of not being able to create along the curved line before

182
00:10:54,279 --> 00:10:58,840
has also been solved in the new version.

183
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:01,320
After creating the smart loop line, click Create.

184
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:03,159
It will automatically create a loop grid.

185
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:08,000
And now we can create a loop grid along the inner line

186
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:14,360
of the support loop points on the floating line updated in the previous version.

187
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:19,919
And if we manually create a loop structure,

188
00:11:19,919 --> 00:11:22,440
we can also duplicate it along the inner line now.

189
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:31,080
In the past, if we wanted to separate the loop surface,

190
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:32,600
we needed to press Ctrl and Shift to do so.

191
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:40,240
In the new version, we can directly separate the loop surface.

192
00:11:42,159 --> 00:11:46,399
Just click Create Loop Line and you can separate it manually.

193
00:11:46,399 --> 00:11:50,680
In the process of separation, if there are five sides or more,

194
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:55,200
that is, there is no way to form a triangle or a quadrilateral structure,

195
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:57,519
this surface will show as orange.

196
00:11:57,519 --> 00:12:00,519
This is to remind you that this is an unusable surface.

197
00:12:00,519 --> 00:12:02,360
We need to continue to separate it again.

198
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:11,039
In the new version, we can now make a frame selection and choose the support point.

199
00:12:11,039 --> 00:12:15,080
Then move or adjust these support points together.

200
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:19,159
If you press the Shift key and then click the frame selection,

201
00:12:19,159 --> 00:12:20,240
you can select more.

202
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:26,240
Press the Ctrl key and the frame selection, you can select less.

203
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:30,159
The new feature is the close combination of the supporting points.

204
00:12:30,159 --> 00:12:32,159
This is the connection in the middle.

205
00:12:32,159 --> 00:12:32,560
Next.

206
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:33,039
Okay.

207
00:12:33,039 --> 00:12:38,039
Here, when I was creating the top, I left some spaces in the middle on purpose.

208
00:12:38,039 --> 00:12:41,039
I didn't do it on purpose.

209
00:12:41,039 --> 00:12:45,039
And here, we choose to make all of them grid.

210
00:12:48,039 --> 00:12:56,039
In the previous version, the structure of our top did not automatically inherit the powder line.

211
00:12:56,039 --> 00:13:00,039
When we export it, we can't merge it.

212
00:13:00,039 --> 00:13:03,039
In the new version, we have a close merge point.

213
00:13:03,039 --> 00:13:07,039
In fact, it is used for the structure after the repackage.

214
00:13:07,039 --> 00:13:12,039
In the new version, we have the function to lock the repackage.

215
00:13:12,039 --> 00:13:19,039
If it is locked, we can only select the original version when we select the version at the 2D window.

216
00:13:19,039 --> 00:13:26,039
If we choose to lock all the version outlines, the outline of the version will be displayed as gray, which means that it cannot be selected.

217
00:13:26,039 --> 00:13:29,039
At this time, we can select the repackage alone.

218
00:13:29,039 --> 00:13:30,039
After that,

219
00:13:30,039 --> 00:13:32,039
we can select the next version.

220
00:13:35,039 --> 00:13:39,039
Now let's separate these two versions and put them together.

221
00:13:40,039 --> 00:13:46,039
Note that we have a pre-preserved point that is not close to the top.

222
00:13:48,039 --> 00:13:54,039
In the previous version, when we export the OBJ file, we will choose the merge point.

223
00:13:54,039 --> 00:13:59,039
The principle of the merge point is that it is based on the powder line to merge.

224
00:13:59,039 --> 00:14:03,039
Therefore, since the structure we export is not based on the powder line,

225
00:14:03,039 --> 00:14:06,039
the top of the top cannot be merged.

226
00:14:06,039 --> 00:14:11,039
In the new version, as long as we choose to merge close to the top,

227
00:14:11,039 --> 00:14:16,039
the top points on the side of the top surface can also be merged.

228
00:14:19,039 --> 00:14:21,039
There is a value here.

229
00:14:21,039 --> 00:14:25,039
This value is as long as the distance between the two points is less than this value.

230
00:14:25,039 --> 00:14:28,039
After we click on the display, you can see that

231
00:14:28,039 --> 00:14:32,039
the top points that have been merged will be shown as red.

232
00:14:32,039 --> 00:14:36,039
In other words, even if your version has a top structure,

233
00:14:36,039 --> 00:14:38,039
the top points will also be merged.

234
00:14:40,039 --> 00:14:44,039
The top points that have not been merged will be shown as blue.

235
00:14:44,039 --> 00:14:49,039
In the previous version, we have a pre-preserved point with some distance.

236
00:14:49,039 --> 00:14:54,039
Now let's reduce the merge distance to 1.

237
00:14:54,039 --> 00:14:57,039
When the distance between the two points is greater than 1,

238
00:14:57,039 --> 00:15:00,039
the merge point will not be merged.

239
00:15:00,039 --> 00:15:02,039
If we need to merge them,

240
00:15:02,039 --> 00:15:06,039
we need to increase the number of merge points.

241
00:15:12,039 --> 00:15:14,039
Then click on Confirm,

242
00:15:14,039 --> 00:15:17,039
and we can export the top structure.

243
00:15:17,039 --> 00:15:21,039
Let's import the OVJ file that we just merged.

244
00:15:21,039 --> 00:15:22,039
Let's take a look at it.

245
00:15:22,039 --> 00:15:24,039
In the previous version, it was merged.

246
00:15:24,039 --> 00:15:27,039
In the previous version, it was merged.

247
00:15:27,039 --> 00:15:29,039
This feature is also for everyone,

248
00:15:29,039 --> 00:15:32,039
to make it convenient for everyone to use it in MMS Designer,

249
